    "narrative": "The heart of the LawDog lineup today rests on the premium matchup against Bieber, who carries a shaky 5.23 xERA into the clash. **Bryce Harper** headlines our production expectations with a 78.75 rating; he\u2019s perfectly positioned in the three-hole to exploit a massive SP skill advantage and a park factor boost. Similarly, **Luis Arraez** (66.78) and speed-threat **Justin Crawford** (66.07) benefit significantly from the soft matchup against the right-hander, with **Justin Crawford**\u2019s utility as an elite stolen base threat keeping him in the mix despite an unfavorable ninth-order penalty. We also see high upside in **Daulton Varsho** (69.59) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (67.47); **Daulton Varsho**\u2019s massive 10% platoon bump against V\u00e1squez creates a ceiling play that makes him a priority start even pending final lineup confirmation.\n\nDeciding the final bench spots required heavy scrutiny, particularly with the bottom end of the order. **Kyle Karros** was the closest to cracking the starting nine with a 48.99 rating, but his limited platoon advantage against McGreevy kept him sidelined in favor of higher-efficiency hitters like **Gavin Sheets**. We are keeping a close watch on **Yainer Diaz** and **Daulton Varsho**, whose scores are currently based on projected lineup spots; should either drop significantly in the order, their efficiency could crater, though their respective matchups against the high-xERA V\u00e1squez currently mitigate that risk. Meanwhile, **Gleyber Torres** and **Jonathan Aranda** face tougher individual tests against Webb and Hancock, respectively. While **Gleyber Torres** enjoys a wind-aided boost, his negative dynamic platoon rating suggests he is a candidate for a late-game swap if the game state warrants a pinch hitter to protect our daily cap.",
